      "message": "fix(sim): judge kept parts at the post by the generation's own law\n\nThe post's live re-judge of kept parts (#1628, kept_rejudge) read every\nkept part by the plain solid law. Generation reads a stock-source Drill,\nBore or Thread by the containment law with the declared holes' modelled\nwalls excused (#1631), and a stock-source cross drill by its radial law\n(#1635). So a legal drill in the part's own hole was refused at the post\non a turned stock: \"S1 now cuts part '<name>'\".\n\nThe re-judge now picks the law as generation does: mark law, hole\ncontainment law (with the same thread grant), cross_part::part_clear,\nelse the solid law. A part-source cross drill also answers to\ncross_part::neighbours_clear, as at generation.\n\nPinned by a_part_added_under_a_stock_source_drill_is_judged_at_the_post_by_the_hole_law:\na part added under a clean stock-source drill posts when it models a hole\nthere and is refused by name when it is solid there.\n\nFixes #1691\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
